Frosted Ginger Pumpkin Spice Cookies
  --Pennant

Cookies:
2 1/2 c flour
1 tsp baking powder
1 tsp baking soda
2 tsp cinnamon
1/2 tsp nutmeg
1/2 c butter, room temp
1/2 tsmp ground ginger
1/2 tsp cloves
1/2 tsp salt
1 c sugar
1/2 c brown sugar
1 c canned pumpkin
1 egg, room temp
1 tsp vanilla
4 oz crystallized ginger, diced

Preheat oven to 350F. Line 2 cookie sheets with parchment paper. Combine flour, baking powder, baking soda, cinnamon, nutmeg, ginger, cloves, and salt in medium bowl;  set aside. /cream together butter and sugars ~2 min, scraping sides of bowl. Add egg. Beat to blend, beat in pumpkin and vanilla; scape down bowl. Gently blend in dry ingredients in 2 batches. Fold in ginger. Drop batter onto cookie sheets by tablespoonfuls. Bake 13-15 min. Cool.

Frosting:
1/2 c butter, room temp
1/2 c cream cheese, softened
2-3 c powdered sugar
1 tsp vanilla
1 tsp cinnamon
1/2 tsp ginger
1/'4 tsp nutmeg

Cream together all ingredients until fluffy. Spread over cooled cookies.
